# will_step_retry — a step on a will's way is carried out by a judged means, and tried again if refused
#
# Lockpicking is a will to unlock a door; from the Test Field its first step is the walk to the yard
# (see will_path.cli). That walk is not what the will wants, so its means is judged like any goal's,
# and the means may refuse it: pinned to Bushcraft, the first willingness answer is "unwilling"
# (--refuse-means 1). A pineal gland of 1 gives the thinking one retry, so the same step comes back
# with a means not yet tried, is carried out — by Hunt, at seed 42 — and reaches the button. The
# will's own goal is never retried this way: a will with Action carries it out itself and cannot
# refuse it.
#
# --means-only bushcraft cannot hold on the retry, whose pool has Bushcraft crossed off; that miss is
# the point, hence allow-flag-miss.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --grant-mm lockpicking,bushcraft --grant-item hairpin --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Field" --period dawn --means-only bushcraft --refuse-means 1 --organs pineal_gland=1

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
observe "Test Yard"
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

advance 12 180
expect-state will "will lockpicking steps=2 first="

click keyword yard
choose 0
choose lockpicking
advance 12 180
expect To get there I must first
expect [Bushcraft
expect That will not do, and I think again
expect another way
expect ] discreetly walk back out into the yard

allow-flag-miss --means-only
quit
